      <!-- 10 FAQs -->
      <section class="section" id="faqs">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>10. FAQs</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="bd">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Does nullable reference types change runtime behavior?</td>
                <td>No. It mainly adds compile-time warnings and changes how you design types (string vs string?).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Should I enable nullable in an old project?</td>
                <td>Yes, but do it module-by-module. Start with DTOs and public APIs.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>When should I use async streams?</td>
                <td>When data arrives over time or is very large (logs, network, paging from DB).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Are default interface methods common in app code?</td>
                <td>More common in libraries/frameworks. Use them carefully in app code.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <div class="tip callout">
            <b>Beginner Tip:</b> If you are confused, build a tiny console demo for each feature. Small examples make the rules clear.
          </div>
